00:50:45,880 --> 00:50:50,880
Certain goods are properly valued in ways other than use.

1120
00:50:50,880 --> 00:50:55,380
What are other ways of valuing and treating

1121
00:50:55,380 --> 00:50:59,880
goods that should not be open to use?

1122
00:50:59,880 --> 00:51:02,880
Anderson says there are many.

1123
00:51:02,880 --> 00:51:03,880
Respect.

1124
00:51:03,880 --> 00:51:04,880
Appreciation.

1125
00:51:05,880 --> 00:51:06,880
Love.

1126
00:51:06,880 --> 00:51:07,880
Honor.

1127
00:51:07,880 --> 00:51:08,880
Awe.

1128
00:51:08,880 --> 00:51:09,880
Sanctity.

1129
00:51:09,880 --> 00:51:14,880
There are many modes of valuation beyond use,

1130
00:51:14,880 --> 00:51:19,880
and certain goods are not properly valued

1131
00:51:19,880 --> 00:51:23,880
if they're treated simply as objects of use.

1132
00:51:24,880 --> 00:51:27,880
How do we go about evaluating that argument of Anderson?

1133
00:51:27,880 --> 00:51:30,380
In a way it takes us back

1134
00:51:30,380 --> 00:51:32,880
to the debate we had with utilitarianism.

1135
00:51:33,880 --> 00:51:34,880
Is use the only way to use?

1136
00:51:35,880 --> 00:51:38,880
Is utility, is use the

1137
00:51:38,880 --> 00:51:41,880
only proper way of treating goods,

1138
00:51:41,880 --> 00:51:48,880
including life, military service, procreation, childbearing?

1139
00:51:48,880 --> 00:51:53,880
And if not, how do we figure out,

1140
00:51:53,880 --> 00:51:58,380
how can we determine what modes of

1141
00:51:58,380 --> 00:52:02,880
valuation are fitting or appropriate to those goods?

1142
00:52:02,880 --> 00:52:04,880
Several years ago there was a scandal surrounding a doctor,

1143
00:52:04,880 --> 00:52:11,880
an infertility specialist in Virginia named Cecil Jacobson.

1144
00:52:11,880 --> 00:52:14,380
He didn't have a donor

1145
00:52:14,380 --> 00:52:16,880
catalog because unknown to his patients,

1146
00:52:16,880 --> 00:52:19,880
all of the sperm he used to

1147
00:52:19,880 --> 00:52:22,880
inseminate his patients came from one donor,

1148
00:52:22,880 --> 00:52:25,880
Dr. Jacobson himself.

1149
00:52:25,880 --> 00:52:29,380
At least one woman who testified in court

1150
00:52:29,380 --> 00:52:32,880
was unnerved at how much her newborn daughter

1151
00:52:32,880 --> 00:52:33,880
looked just like him.

1152
00:52:33,880 --> 00:52:39,380
Now it's possible to condemn Dr. Jacobson

1153
00:52:39,380 --> 00:52:44,880
for failing to inform the women in advance.

1154
00:52:44,880 --> 00:52:47,880
That would be the argument about consent.

1155
00:52:47,880 --> 00:52:50,380
The columnist Ellen Goodman described

1156
00:52:50,380 --> 00:52:52,880
the bizarre scenario as follows.

1157
00:52:52,880 --> 00:52:55,880
Dr. Jacobson, she wrote, gave

1158
00:52:55,880 --> 00:52:58,880
his infertility business the personal touch.

1159
00:52:58,880 --> 00:53:01,880
But now the rest of us, she wrote,

1160
00:53:01,880 --> 00:53:05,380
are in for a round

1161
00:53:05,380 --> 00:53:08,880
of second thoughts about sperm donation.

1162
00:53:08,880 --> 00:53:11,380
Goodman concluded that fatherhood

1163
00:53:11,380 --> 00:53:13,880
should be something you do,

1164
00:53:13,880 --> 00:53:15,880
not something you donate.

1165
00:53:15,880 --> 00:53:17,880
And I think what she was doing,

1166
00:53:17,880 --> 00:53:21,880
and what the philosopher Elizabeth Anderson is doing,

1167
00:53:21,880 --> 00:53:24,380
and what Andrew was suggesting

1168
00:53:24,380 --> 00:53:26,880
with his argument about dehumanization,

1169
00:53:26,880 --> 00:53:30,880
is pondering whether there are certain goods,

1170
00:53:30,880 --> 00:53:32,880
that money shouldn't buy,

1171
00:53:32,880 --> 00:53:34,880
not just because of tainted consent,

1172
00:53:34,880 --> 00:53:39,380
but also perhaps because certain goods are properly

1173
00:53:39,380 --> 00:53:43,880
valued in a way higher than mere use.

1174
00:53:43,880 --> 00:53:45,380
Those at least are the

1175
00:53:45,380 --> 00:53:46,880
questions we are going to pursue

1176
00:53:46,880 --> 00:53:48,880
with the help of some

1177
00:53:48,880 --> 00:53:50,880
philosophers in the weeks to come.

